STARTER Configurable Adapter
============================

1. OVERVIEW
===========

starter-configurable-adapter (STCA) is an independent HTTP process that
loads one plugin to talk to an external source and exposes a common
numeric JSON API for configurable-service. This tree ships the core and
the in-tree `dummy` example plugin; product plugins (e.g. Ariston) are
separate repositories (one plugin per repo).

Read path:

  plugin  →  signal data-ready (GHashTable)  →  adapter memory  →  GET /data
  →  configurable-service  →  starter STInput

Write path:

  starter STOutput  →  configurable-service  →  PUT/POST /data
  →  stca_plugin_write_value(s)  →  external source

For the technical manual (concepts + configuration/HTTP reference):

    $ make -C doc info   # Info
    $ make doc           # PDF (needs TeX)

2. PREREQUISITES
================

* GLib 2.0 / GObject / GIO / GModule (libglib2.0-dev)
* libxml2 (libxml2-dev)
* json-glib (libjson-glib-dev)
* libsoup 3.x or 2.4 >= 2.58 (libsoup-3.0-dev or libsoup2.4-dev)
* Autotools (autoconf, automake, libtool)
* Texinfo (makeinfo) to build the manual; TeX for PDF

3. BUILDING FROM SOURCE
=======================

    $ ./autogen.sh
    $ ./configure
    $ make
    $ sudo make install

4. RUNNING
==========

    $ starter-configurable-adapter --config /path/to/adapter.stca.xml

See examples/dummy/ for a temporary plugin that exercises the HTTP API.
Out-of-tree plugins are built separately and loaded with `--plugin-dir`.
Details are in the Texinfo manual.

